# The AND/OR fixture: hledger's line-prefix `&`, in every layout it occurs in.
#
# A matcher line beginning `&` is AND-ed onto the line above it, and a plain
# line starts a fresh OR branch, so a block's matchers are an OR of AND-groups.
# Verified against the hledger 1.52 binary, not the manual — `just rules-check`
# drives hledger from `and-groups.csv` beside this file, and
# `crates/ledgeline-core/tests/rules_hledger_render.rs` asserts hledger routes
# each row the way this file's groups say it should.

skip 1
fields date, description, amount, card
date-format %Y-%m-%d
currency $
account1 assets:bank:checking
account2 expenses:unknown

# An AND chain under an INLINE header: the header's own matcher heads the group
# and the `&` line continues it, so BOTH must match.
if AMAZON
& %card personal
    account2 expenses:shopping:online

# An OR of two AND-groups, stacked. `(GROCER and personal)` or
# `(FARMERS and business)` — the shape the whole feature exists for.
if
GROCER
& %card personal
FARMERS
& %card business
    account2  expenses:food:groceries
    comment   weekly shop

# A plain OR list, which is one matcher per group. It is here so the fixture
# proves the two shapes coexist in one file rather than being alternatives.
if
SHELL
CHEVRON
    account2 expenses:auto:fuel

# hledger's OTHER spelling of the same AND: `&&` in the middle of ONE line.
# Verified against 1.52 — the split is unconditional and needs no surrounding
# whitespace, and each piece keeps its own `%field` scope. Row 9 (business)
# must land here and row 10 (personal) must not; a reader that took this for an
# OR would take both.
if %description TARGET && %card business
    account2 expenses:shopping:target

# The two spellings composed. Line 2's leading `&` continues the group line 1
# opened, and that same line's own `&&` splits it further, so this is ONE group
# of three: STAPLES and business and -85. Rows 11, 12 and 13 differ in exactly
# one of the three, so only row 11 may land here.
if
STAPLES
& %card business && %amount -85
    account2 expenses:office:supplies
